Please note, handling security and regulatory requirements such as transaction replay prevention could be handled at a higher layer in the system or by a separate service, depending on your architecture. This class only handles low-level random number generation logic. 

Also, please take into account that `std::mt19937` is not cryptographically secure, if you need such guarantee consider using `<random>` header's `std::default_random_engine` or `std::random_device` for higher security needs.
