['Here's a sample code which might help you start with this task. However, please remember this is just a skeleton code and does not include all features mentioned in the requirements (like network integration or custom comparison logic). 

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class DisjointPairs {

    private static final int MAX_ARRAY_SIZE = 10000000; // Max array size is set to 10M elements as per requirement

    // This map will contain disjoint pairs for every thread.
    private ConcurrentHashMap<Long, AtomicInteger> disjointPairsCount = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public int countDisjointPairs(int[] arr) {
        if (arr == null || arr.length > MAX_ARRAY_SIZE) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid input array");
        }

        long threadId = Thread.currentThread().getId(); // get current thread id
        disjointPairsCount.putIfAbsent(threadId, new AtomicInteger()); // initialize count for this thread if not already done 

        ForkJoinPool customThreadPool = new ForkJoinPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors()); // use custom thread pool to control concurrency level and optimize resource usage

        // The task is a recursive action which splits the array into smaller tasks until it can be solved directly (i.e., when the problem size becomes small enough)
        customThreadPool.invoke(new CountDisjointTask(arr, 0, arr.length - 1));

        // Aggregate all counts from all threads and return total count of disjoint pairs.
        int totalCount = disjointPairsCount.values().stream()
                .mapToInt(AtomicInteger::get)
                .sum();

        customThreadPool.shutdown(); // shutdown thread pool once we are done with it

        return totalCount;
    }

    private class CountDisjointTask extends RecursiveAction {

        private int[] arr;
        private int start, end;

        public CountDisjointTask(int[] arr, int start, int end) {
            this.arr = arr;
            this.start = start;
            this.end = end;
        }

        @Override
        protected void compute() {
            if (end - start <= 1) { // base case where problem can be solved directly
                checkDisjointAndUpdateCount(arr[start], arr[end]);
            } else {
                int mid = (start + end) / 2;

                CountDisjointTask task1 = new CountDisjointTask(arr, start, mid); // divide problem into two sub-problems
                CountDisjointTask task2 = new CountDisjointTask(arr, mid + 1, end);

                invokeAll(task1, task2); // solve the sub-problems in parallel
            }
        }

        private void checkDisjointAndUpdateCount(int a, int b) {
            if (gcd(a, b) == 1) {  // update count for disjoint pairs using gcd function
                disjointPairsCount.get(Thread.currentThread().getId()).incrementAndGet();
            }
        }

        private static int gcd(int a, int b) { // function to calculate greatest common divisor
            if (b == 0) return a;
            else return gcd(b, a % b);
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses the ForkJoin framework for concurrency and implements a divide-and-conquer approach using RecursiveAction to handle large arrays. However, this is a simplified version of the problem and does not include some parts like network integration or custom comparison logic as per the detailed requirements.
']

['Below is an example of how you might begin implementing such a service using Java NIO. It's important to note that this is just the beginning, and you would need to add much more functionality for it to meet all your requirements.

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.ByteBuffer;
import java.nio.channels.*;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.Set;

public class ConnectionManager {
    private Selector selector;

    public void startConnection(String hostname, int port) throws IOException {
        SocketChannel client = SocketChannel.open(new InetSocketAddress(hostname, port));
        client.configureBlocking(false);
        selector = Selector.open();
        client.register(selector, SelectionKey.OP_READ | SelectionKey.OP_WRITE);
    }

    public void manageConnections() throws IOException {
        while (true) {
            int readyChannels = selector.selectNow();
            if(readyChannels == 0) continue;

            Set<SelectionKey> selectedKeys = selector.selectedKeys();
            Iterator<SelectionKey> keyIterator = selectedKeys.iterator();

            while (keyIterator.hasNext()) {
                SelectionKey key  = keyIterator.next();

                if(key.isAcceptable()) {
                    // Register a new connection
                } else if (key.isConnectable()) {
                    // Connection established
                } else if (key.isReadable()) {
                    read((SocketChannel) key.channel());
                } else if (key.isWritable()) {
                    write((SocketChannel) key.channel(), "Message");
                }

                keyIterator.remove();
            }
        }
    }

    private void read(SocketChannel client) throws IOException {
        ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.allocate(256);
        client.read(buffer);

        String response = new String(buffer.array()).trim();
        System.out.println("Response: " + response);
    }

    private void write(SocketChannel client, String msg) throws IOException {
        ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.wrap(msg.getBytes());
        client.write(buffer);

        if (!buffer.hasRemaining()) System.out.println("Message sent: " + msg);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        ConnectionManager manager = new ConnectionManager();
        manager.startConnection("localhost", 5000);
        manager.manageConnections();
    }
}
```
