```php
<?php
// Include the necessary files
require_once('DBInterface.php');
require_once('APIClient.php');
require_once('Logger.php');

class ClinicStatusService {
    private $db;
    private $apiClient;
    private $logger;
    private $semaphore;

    function __construct() {
        $this->db = new DBInterface();
        $this->apiClient = new APIClient();
        $this->logger = new Logger();
        // Initialize a semaphore for synchronization
        $this->semaphore = sem_get(ftok(__FILE__, 's'));
    }

    public function updateClinicStatus($clinicID, $ipAddress) {
        if (sem_acquire($this->semaphore)) {
            try {
                // Get the clinic's current status from external API
                $status = $this->apiClient->getCurrentClinicStatus($clinicID);
                // If status fetched successfully, update it in the database
                if (isset($status)) {
                    $success = $this->db->updateClinic($clinicID, $ipAddress, $status);
                    // Log the result of the update
                    if (!$success) {
                        $this->logger->log("Failed to update clinic: " . $clinicID);
                    } else {
                        $this->logger->log("Successfully updated clinic: " . $clinicID);
                    }
                } else {
                    $this->logger->log("Failed to fetch status for clinic: " . $clinicID);
                }
            } catch (Exception $e) {
                $this->logger->log($e->getMessage());
            } finally {
                sem_release($this->semaphore);
            }
        } else {
            $this->logger->log("Failed to acquire lock for clinic: " . $clinicID);
        }
    }
}
?>
```
This solution includes a `DBInterface` class for database operations, an `APIClient` class for interaction with the external API, and a `Logger` class for logging updates. It uses PHP's semaphore functions for synchronization to ensure thread safety when handling concurrent requests from multiple clinics. Please note that actual implementation would be much more complicated considering error handling, data validation, response formatting, etc.
