['The Java solution involves the use of several libraries such as JSch for SSH connections, Apache Commons IO for file handling, Apache HttpClient for API calls, etc. Please note that you will have to implement this task in a full development environment with a build system like Maven or Gradle, and run it on an actual remote server for real testing.

Below is a high-level example of how your code structure might look:

```java
public class SSHExecutor {
    private JSch jsch;

    public SSHExecutor() {
        // Initialize JSCH library
        this.jsch = new JSch();

        // Load private key file
        File keyFile = new File("path_to_private_key");
        if(keyFile.exists()) {
            jsch.addIdentity("path_to_private_key");
        } else {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Private key not found");
        }
    }

    // Establish SSH Connection with a server and execute commands
    public void executeCommands(String host, String username, List<String> commands) throws JSchException, IOException {
        Session session = jsch.getSession(username, host, 22);

        // Create an exec channel for command execution
        ChannelExec channel = (ChannelExec) session.openChannel("exec");

        // Execute each command in the list
        for(String command : commands) {
            channel.setCommand(command);

            InputStream commandOutput = channel.getInputStream();
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(commandOutput));

            // Handle output and error streams
            String line;
            while((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
To achieve all your requirements, you would need to extend this code with additional functionality for each requirement as described above and integrate it in a full application architecture that takes care of concurrency, error handling, configuration management, and more. Also consider using libraries like Apache Camel or Spring Integration which can help manage these tasks.
