["Here is a simplified version of how you might implement a session management microservice in PHP using OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, custom protocols and external APIs. Due to the complexity and requirements mentioned in your task, this code block will only provide a skeleton structure for the project which needs further development according to specific business rules and functionalities.

```php
<?php
namespace App\Services;

use App\Models\Session;
use Predis\ClientInterface;
use GuzzleHttp\Client as HttpClient;
use Illuminate\Contracts\Cache\Repository as Cache;
use Psr\Log\LoggerInterface;
use Symfony\Component\RateLimiter\RateLimiterFactory;

class SessionService
{
    private $client;
    private $cache;
    private $logger;
    private $rateLimiterFactory;

    public function __construct(HttpClient $client, Cache $cache, LoggerInterface $logger, RateLimiterFactory $rateLimiterFactory)
    {
        $this->client = $client;
        $this->cache = $cache;
        $this->logger = $logger;
        $this->rateLimiterFactory = $rateLimiterFactory;
    }

    public function createSession(array $data)
    {
        try{
            $limiter = $this->rateLimiterFactory->create($data['user_id']);
            if (false === $limiter->consume()->isAccepted()) {
                throw new \Exception('Too many requests');
            }

            $response = $this->client->request('POST', 'auth/token', ['json' => $data]);

            if($response->getStatusCode() === 201) {
                $body = json_decode((string) $response->getBody(), true);
                $session = new Session();
                $session->user_id = $data['user_id'];
                $session->token = $body['access_token'];
                //... set other session properties based on the response from auth/token endpoint

                return $this->cache->remember('session:' . $session->id, 60 * 24 * 30, function () use ($session) {
                    return $session;
                });
            }
        } catch (\Exception $e){
            $this->logger->error($e->getMessage());
            throw new \RuntimeException('Failed to create session');
        }
    }

    //... other methods for managing, validating and terminating sessions
}
``` 
Please note that implementing this service might require a good understanding of PHP programming, various APIs (GuzzleHttp, Predis), logging (PSR-3), rate limiting (symfony/rate-limiter) and cache. This code block is only the first step towards creating the microservice you asked for and it needs to be further extended based on your requirements.
