class IdentityProvider {
    private $provider;

    public function __construct($clientId, $clientSecret, $redirectUri) {
        $this->provider = new OAuth2Client([
            'clientId'                => $clientId, 
            'clientSecret'            => $clientSecret,
            'redirectUri'             => $redirectUri,
        ]);
    }

    public function getAuthorizationUrl() {
        $authorizationUrl = $this->provider->getAuthorizationUrl();

        // Store the state somewhere to validate in callback.php
        $_SESSION['oauth2state'] = $this->provider->getState();

        return $authorizationUrl;
    }

    public function getUserInfo($code) {
        $token = $this->provider->getAccessToken('authorization_code', ['code' => $code]);
        try {
            $response = $this->provider->getResourceOwner($token)->toArray();
            return $response;
        } catch (RequestException $e) {
            // Handle network failures, rate limiting, invalid tokens etc.
        }
    }
}
```
This class manages the OAuth 2.0 authentication process with an external identity provider. The `getAuthorizationUrl` method returns a URL that users should be redirected to for authentication and authorization. After successful login, they will be redirected back to your application with an authorization code, which can be exchanged for an access token using the `getUserInfo` method.

