Here's some rough skeleton code:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.security.*;
import javax.crypto.*;
import com.jcraft.jsch.*;

public class Main {
    private static final String PRIVATE_KEY = "path/to/private/key";

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        JSch jsch = new JSch();

        // Load the private key
        KeyPair kpair = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance("RSA");
        SecureRandom random = SecureRandom.getInstance("SHA1PRNG", "SUN");
        kpair.initialize(2048, random);

        jsch.addIdentity(PRIVATE_KEY);

        // Establish an SSH connection
        Session session = jsch.getSession("username", "hostname", 22);
        session.connect();

        // Execute commands on remote servers concurrently
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);
        List<Future<String>> results = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
            Future<String> result = executor.submit(() -> executeCommand("command", session));
            results.add(result);
        }

        // Handle command execution errors
        try {
            for (Future<String> result : results) {
                System.out.println(result.get());
            }
        } catch (ExecutionException | InterruptedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }

        // Delete local files and manage thread-safe operations for LTE MME message file creation/modification
        Files.deleteIfExists(Paths.get("path/to/local/file"));

        executor.shutdown();
    }

    private static String executeCommand(String command, Session session) {
        try {
            ChannelExec channel = (ChannelExec) session.openChannel("exec");

            channel.setCommand(command);
            channel.connect();

            InputStream in = channel.getInputStream();
            byte[] tmp = new byte[1024];
            while (true) {
                while (in.available() > 0) {
                    int i = in.read(tmp, 0, 1024);
                    if (i < 0) break;

                    System.out.print(new String(tmp, 0, i));
                }

                if (channel.isClosed()) {
                    if (in.available() > 0) continue;

                    System.out.println("exit-status: " + channel.getExitStatus());
                    break;
                }

                try { Thread.sleep(1000); } catch (Exception ee) {}
            }

            channel.disconnect();
        } catch (JSchException | IOException ex) {
            ex.printStackTrace();
        }

        return "";
    }
}
```
This code demonstrates SSH connections, command execution concurrently and file deletion operations. However, it doesn't include all the requirements in your problem statement. 

In order to fully meet all the criteria you specified (including handling external dependencies, designing caching mechanisms, implementing a backpressure mechanism, retry mechanism, memory-efficient data structure, load balancing strategies etc), a larger application would be needed that uses many different components and packages such as Spring Boot, Java Executor Services, Apache Commons Pool for the Memory pool allocator, Netflix Hystrix for Circuit Breakers, OkHttp or Retrofit for API calls, JMX for monitoring resources, Guava Cache for caching, etc. 

Please note that writing this kind of application would need extensive understanding of many areas of software engineering and could take considerable time to implement correctly and thoroughly test.
